  "notes": "You can hear it long before you reach the roadworks.\n\nThis measurement captures an excavator-mounted hydraulic breaker breaking the road surface at close range. What surprised me wasn’t only the level — around 100 dB during the measurement — but how persistent the sound remained and how clearly it could still be heard well beyond the immediate work area.\n\nThe workers nearby were wearing hearing protection, and for good reason: at these levels, duration becomes as important as loudness. For a pedestrian, the exposure may last only seconds; for the people operating the machinery, it can be part of an entire working day.\n\nA striking example of how one relatively localised source can temporarily change the acoustic environment of a much larger part of a city street.",
